    "title": "Legislators Operating Clothing Drive for Women - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Pam Robinson ,\n8 hours ago Legislators Stephanie Bontempi, Leslie Kennedy, Rebecca Sanin, Trish Bergin, and Ann Welker,\nThe five “Ladies of the Legislature” are working together during March to help women in need of professional and casual clothing.\nLegislators Leslie Kennedy, Trish Bergin, Stephanie Bontempi, Ann Welker, and Rebecca Sanin (LD-16), with their respective staff, are conducting a drive for clothing and such accessories as gently used shoes and handbags.\nThe donations will be delivered to organizations around the county to help give those women in need an improved self-image and a greater sense of independence in a time when hard-working families are beset by economic difficulties. Clothing will be collected at each of the five District Offices throughout March, which is Women’s History Month.\nBontempi’s office is at 224 Wall St #303, Huntington.\nSanin’s office is at 315 Walt Whitman Rd, Huntington Station.\nBontempi Legislation Tightens Animal Abuse Penalties\nBontempi, Sanin Honor Residents for Contributions to Community\nRenovations Coming to Five Corners Intersection in Huntington Station\nTurkey Alternatives for Vegans and Vegetarians\nBus Service to Return to New York Avenue Route\nWhitman Students Explore Service Opportunities at Nonprofit Volunteer Fair",
    "summary": "8 hours ago Legislators Stephanie Bontempi, Leslie Kennedy, Rebecca Sanin, Trish Bergin, and Ann Welker, The five “Ladies of the Legislature” are working together during March to help women in need of professional and casual clothing. Legislators Leslie Kennedy, Trish Bergin, Stephanie Bontempi, Ann Welker, and Rebecca Sanin (LD-16), with their respective staff, are conducting a drive for clothing and such accessories as gently used shoes and handbags.",
